<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ declines to comment on SIA link.</title>
<headline>Air NZ declines to comment on SIA link.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air New Zealand Ltd spokesman Cameron Hill said on Monday the company would not comment on speculation that it would soon enter an alliance with Singapore Airlines and Ansett International.</p>
<p>&quot;We talk to other airlines all the time,&quot; Hill said.</p>
<p>Monday's issue of the Australian Financial Review said an Air NZ, Ansett, SIA alliance was imminent. Such a tie-up would pose a threat to the Qantas Airways Ltd -British Airways Plc link on routes between Australia and Europe, the paper said.</p>
<p>Ansett is 50/50 owned by News Corp Ltd and Air NZ.  </p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
